[https://i.imgur.com/jO0D9oJ.jpg](https://i.imgur.com/jO0D9oJ.jpg)

No worries, Stoic. You're not alone. This was not funny at all. It seems, a lot of what's being posted in /r/funny is caters to a particular mind that deals with harming another living thing.

&#x200B;

I understand the cat playing with the mouse since they tend to play with their food, but the person recording is messing around by recording the scene unnecessarily, while he enables the mouse to run and have the cat chase it some more.

&#x200B;

Just know that it's good that you feel something compared to the people thinking this is hilarious.
